d.themes=[['People expect jobs to be cut once the claims triage tool is fully rolled out.','fear','most',['Claims Processing','Customer Service','Policy Administration'],['Everyone says it will free up time. Nobody says whose time.','They said the same thing before the last restructure.'],[_triage],'Raised in every session with frontline teams. People hear that the tool will free up time, but nobody says whose time, and many connect it with last spring\'s restructure of the claims queues, which was described the same way. The worry is strongest in Claims Processing, where the tool is already in use.'],['Customer service staff fear being scored against what the AI assistant would have done.','fear','often',['Customer Service','Claims Processing'],['My numbers are now compared with what the assistant would have done.','If I rewrite its reply, my score goes down, even when its reply was wrong.'],[_chat],'Agents say their handling figures are now compared with the reply-drafting assistant\'s suggestions. Some say that rewriting a reply the assistant got wrong counts against them, so they feel pushed to send replies they disagree with.'],['Underwriters worry they will have to defend decisions they cannot explain.','fear','often',['Underwriting'],['If the score says no and I cannot say why, I still have to tell the broker.','I am the one who signs it, but I am not the one who decided.'],[_risk],'When the risk score declines a case, the underwriter still has to give the broker a reason. Underwriters say they sign decisions they did not make and cannot fully explain, and that this leaves them personally exposed.'],['People believe there is a headcount target behind the AI plan that leadership has not shared.','notTold','most',['Claims Processing','Underwriting','Customer Service','Policy Administration'],['There is a number somewhere. We just have not been told it.','Why else would they track how much time the tool saves per person?'],[_triage,_chat],'Many believe a number of roles to be cut already exists, and point to the tracking of time saved per person as the evidence. No one has said there is no such target, so the silence is read as confirmation.'],['Underwriters and analysts believe they are not told how much the risk score drives pricing.','notTold','few',['Underwriting','Pricing and Analytics'],['Nobody will tell us how much weight the postcode carries.'],[_risk],'Raised by a few people in Underwriting and in Pricing and Analytics. They want to know how much weight factors such as the postcode carry, and suspect the answer is kept from them on purpose.'],['People would trust the strategy if they had a written promise about their roles before each rollout.','trust','often',['Claims Processing','Customer Service','Policy Administration'],['Put in writing what happens to my job, before the tool arrives.','Tell us before, not after.'],[],'People asked for something in writing, given before a tool arrives, that says what will happen to their role. Being told afterward, as happened with the queue restructure, is what they do not want repeated.'],['People would trust the strategy if they could challenge an AI result without it being held against them.','trust','often',['Claims Processing','Underwriting','Legal and Compliance'],['I want to say the model is wrong and not have it held against me.','Show us that someone listened the last time we flagged a problem.'],[_triage,_risk],'Adjusters and underwriters want a recognized way to say that a model is wrong. They also want to see that the last problem they flagged was listened to, since two recent concerns about the triage tool got no response.']].map(function(t){return {id:culNew('themes'),theme:t[0],question:t[1],widespread:t[2],teams:t[3].map(function(n){return _tc[n]}),examples:(Array.isArray(t[4])?t[4]:[t[4]]).filter(Boolean).map(function(x){return {id:newId('tx'),text:x}}),uses:t[5],description:t[6]||''}});
/* 7 Oct 2026 (Batch 3, step 2.1): the demo target. Eleven dimension targets (priorities 1, 2, 4, 7), a decision on every seeded value and commitment, two new values, one new commitment, a response to every seeded theme, and the new culture statement. Links use ids captured in variables; rows are stored as the app stores them (rowSettings.row a number, row lists strings). No completion is seeded. */
d.rowSettings=[[1,'Claims handlers and underwriters tell their manager when a tool\'s result looks wrong, and nobody is criticized for it. When a colleague makes a mistake, the team talks about how to fix it before it talks about who made it.',4.0,true],[2,'Teams run small AI experiments without asking permission when the cost is within the agreed budget. They write up and discuss a failed experiment instead of hiding it.',3.8,true],[3,'Employees say openly which AI tools they use in their work. A manager judges work done with AI help by the same standard as other work.',4.0,false],[4,'When an adjuster or underwriter questions an AI result, the question is recorded and someone with authority answers it. Meetings include time for dissenting views before a decision is made.',4.0,true],[5,'Senior leaders use AI in their own work and describe what went well and what went wrong at all-staff briefings. They follow the same rules they set for others.',3.8,false],[6,'Reviews and bonuses give credit for trying something new, for raising a problem early and for working across teams, not only for volume of output.',3.6,false],[7,'Leaders tell employees before a rollout what will change in their roles, and they answer questions about jobs directly. Employees can say what AI means for their own role.',4.0,true],[8,'A person with a name makes every decision that affects a member or an employee, and can explain it without saying only that the model decided. Teams review how they used AI at regular intervals.',4.0,false],[9,'Legal and Compliance join an AI project when it starts, not when it is close to launch. Pricing and Analytics get the underwriting information they need within days.',3.6,false],[10,'Before a new AI tool goes live, the team writes down its effect on the people who will use it or be affected by it, and changes the plan where the effect is harmful.',3.8,false],[11,'No team is asked to take on more change than it can absorb. When a team\'s estimated load goes above 100%, the plan says what will be paused or moved.',3.4,false]].map(function(x){return {id:culNew('rowSettings'),row:x[0],targetDescription:x[1],targetScore:x[2],priority:x[3]}});
