/* ═══ Paul (19 Oct 2026): the charter as promises, owners and evidence. A commitment (chCommits) holds the promise, its owner and the work that delivers it; each charter entry is one of its measures, with a target per quarter. Practice Counts and the other readers keep reading charter entries, one per measure. ═══ */
var CUL_ROW_DESC={1:'People can raise problems, admit mistakes, and disagree without fear of how it will reflect on them.',2:'People can try new ways of working, including with AI, and a well-run experiment that fails is accepted.',3:'People say openly when and how they use AI, and work done with AI is judged fairly.',4:'Concerns and bad news reach the people who need to hear them, and get a response.',5:'Leaders behave the way they ask others to behave, including in their own use of AI.',6:'The behaviors the organization says it wants are the ones it assesses and rewards.',7:'People hear plainly what AI means for their roles: what is decided, what is not, and what support they will get.',8:'People'+"\u2019"+'s judgment still counts where AI is involved, and they can question or override what it recommends.',9:'Problems that need several teams get those teams working together without delay.',10:'Decisions about AI tools take account of their effect on people and how they work.',11:'The amount of change each team is asked to absorb at once is manageable.'};
var CUL_ROW_EXAMPLES={1:'You might count the mistakes teams wrote up and discussed in their reviews, or the concerns raised through a formal channel that received a written answer.',2:'You might count the managers running a micro-charter, the small AI experiments started, or the experiments written up whatever their result.',3:'You might count the show-the-work sessions held, or the pieces of work submitted with AI use stated, where the organization asks for it.',4:'You might count the concerns answered within the set response time, or the problems reported early by the people closest to the work.',5:'You might count the times a senior leader told a wider group how they use AI in their own work, or about a mistake they made with it.',6:'You might count the reviews that used the new evaluation criteria, or the recognitions given for the behaviors in the target culture.',7:'You might count the roles whose people have been told in writing what is changing, or the decisions about roles announced within a set time of being made.',8:'You might count the recorded overrides of an AI recommendation, or the meetings in which a team reviewed which AI output it accepted or overruled.',9:'You might count the working sessions with people from at least two functions, or the requests for help between functions answered within a week.',10:'You might count the AI deployment reviews completed, or the AI decisions in which front-line staff were consulted before approval.',11:'You might count the teams absorbing more changes than the agreed limit, or the changes postponed to keep a team within it.'}; /* Paul (20 Oct 2026): examples for every dimension, in a fold, instead of ready-made measures */
