  batt:"Review each AI use for what it does to your culture, decide whether it goes ahead, and commit to asking the question every time.",
  carousel:{
    why:{h:"Ask what each AI deployment does to the culture.",b:"Most AI decisions are made on cost, speed, and risk. The effect on culture rarely comes up, even though it decides whether people trust the AI and use it well. A deployment can work as designed and still weaken trust or the skills people rely on. Asking about culture before and during a deployment lets you see such effects early.",example:"In their Fast Company article [Culture Is Where AI Strategy Goes to Die](https://www.fastcompany.com/91537924/ai-work-culture-strategy-90-day-plan) (May 11, 2026), Faisal Hoque and Paul Scade ask that every major AI initiative be reviewed with three questions about its effect on culture."},
    what:{h:"Three questions and a decision for each AI use.",b:"The step lists every AI use recorded in step 1.1 and marks the ones that must be reviewed. Each review asks three questions about the effect on culture and judges how well each answer fits the culture you want. It then records what to weigh before deciding, such as the change load on the teams affected and whether people are ready. It ends with a decision. Each completed review can be printed as an AI Deployment Review."},
    how:{h:"Answer in plain words, then decide.",b:"Start with the uses already in operation, then apply the review to new ones. For each question, write what you see and choose whether it is a “Good fit,” “Acceptable,” or a “Poor fit” with the culture you want. The manager of the team most affected takes part as the human in the room. If an answer is not a clear yes, add a note saying what is missing."},
    outcome:{h:"A deployment review for every AI use that needs one.",b:"You leave with a completed review for every AI use that had to be reviewed, each ending in a decision."}},
  tabs:{a:"Deployments to Review",b:"The Deployment Review",c:"Charter Entry"},
  secIntro:{
    a:"These are the AI uses recorded in step 1.1. Uses that must be reviewed are marked. Open a use to review it, or add a use that is not yet listed.",
    b:"Review one AI use at a time, in five parts. Part 2 appears only for uses that change what people do or decide. Fill in every field in each part that appears.",
    c:"This entry is for Culture in AI decisions. Write the commitment to ask the culture question of every AI deployment. Then choose how you will check that the commitment is kept."},
  a:{note:"A use must be reviewed when its status is In use or Pilot and it takes over tasks people did, makes or shapes decisions about people, or replaces roles. Other uses may be reviewed but do not have to be. A Planned use that changes work in one of these ways needs a review before it can move to Pilot or In use.",
    empty:"No AI uses are recorded yet. Add a use here, or record it in step 1.1.",
    chipMust:"Must be reviewed",chipOpt:"Optional",stateNone:"Not started",statePart:"In progress",stateDone:"Review complete",
    btnReview:"Open review",btnAdd:"Add an AI use",addPurpose:"This creates a new record with the same fields as step 1.1. It will also appear there.",
    missUse:'AI Uses: "{use}" still needs a completed deployment review.',missNone:"AI Uses: add an AI use, or tick in step 1.1 that the organization has no AI in use or planned.",
    fromLanding:"From step 1.1 Assessment Battery"},
  b:{startHead:"Start a review",startHelp:"Choose an AI use. Each use has one review.",startBtn:"Start review",empty:"No AI uses are available to review. Add one in Deployments to Review.",
    purpose:["Answer each question in a few sentences, then choose a verdict.","Separate the work that processes information from the work that engages with the people affected.","Ask what this deployment says about the organization, and whether the people involved are ready.","Ask what the AI use takes for granted, and whether that fits the culture you want.","Record what was decided, by whom, and which dimensions the review bears on."],
    heads:["Part 1: Three questions about the effect on culture","Part 2: Human in the room","Part 3: Identity and readiness","Part 4: Imported assumptions","Part 5: The decision"],
    gloss:["Describe the effect you can see or expect on how people work, decide, and treat one another.","Think about whether people are gaining skill and confidence, or losing them.","Think about how the organization is carrying out the deployment, including how fast and whom it asked."],
    helpAnswer:"Write a few sentences.",noteTransp:"Note on the transparency test",noteReady:"What is missing",noteFit:"Note on fit",
    hirHelp:"Name the manager of the team most affected, by role and not by name. This person takes part in the review as the human in the room.",
    roomHidden:"Part 2 applies only to uses that take over tasks people did, make or shape decisions about people, or replace roles. It is not needed for this use.",
    overrideTitle:"From step 2.3 Rewards and Protections: override rule",overrideIntro:"Check the decision against the override rule recorded in step 2.3 before you finish.",
    sumHead:"All reviews",sumPurpose:"This summary shows the three verdicts and the decision for every review.",sumEmpty:"No reviews have been started.",
    miss:'The Deployment Review: "{use}" Part {n} still needs {list}.',
    complete:"Complete",fieldsToFill:"{n} fields to fill",fieldsToFill1:"1 field to fill",chooseVerdict:"Choose a verdict",choose:"Choose an answer",chooseDecision:"Choose a decision"},
  c:{req:"",intro:"This entry is for Culture in AI decisions. Write the commitment to ask the culture question of every AI deployment. Then choose how you will check that the commitment is kept."},
  out:{title:"AI Deployment Review: {use}",lead:"A review of what this AI deployment is doing to the organization's culture, and the decision that followed.",desc:"A completed deployment review of one AI use, with the answers to every part and the decision.",none:"No review is complete yet.",pick:"Choose a completed review.",sec:["The AI use","Effect on culture","Human in the room","Identity and readiness","Imported assumptions","Decision"]},
  /* ruled: the question labels and the Part 5 field labels, from brief 13 */
  q:{map:"Map the work. Which parts are processing tasks, and which involve engaging with the people affected?",better:"Where does AI do the processing better?",needs:"What does the human need in order to engage with the people affected for real?",transparency:"The transparency test. If the people affected knew how the decision was made, would they feel engaged with, or managed by a machine?",says:"What does this deployment say about who we are?",ready:"Are the leaders and staff involved ready for the change?",assumptions:"What assumptions about evidence, risk, and people does this tool bring with it?",fit:"Do they fit the target culture?"},
